<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port reopens - sources.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port reopens - sources.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea reopened early on Tuesday after a 42-hour closure because of bad weather, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>The port reopened at 0800 (local) on Tuesday as high winds and waves subsided, the sources said.</p>
<p>Tankers were alongside berths one and two loading Russian Urals crude on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Oil terminals at Odessa and Tuapse, also on the Black Sea, were working normally as was Latvia's port of Ventspils on the Baltic.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
